---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Support | parry"
  description="Get help with parry. Email support@parryai.app, manage your subscription, restore a Pro purchase, or delete your data from inside the app."
  canonicalPath="/support"
>
  <section class="px-6 py-20 md:px-10 md:py-28 lg:px-14">
    <div class="prose-legal mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="font-display mb-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-5xl" style="letter-spacing: -0.025em;">parry support</h1>
      <p class="mb-12 text-lg text-text-secondary">
        parry is an AI-powered app for replying to text messages. Paste a message, pick a tone, and get ready-to-send suggestions. Need help? Start here.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:support@parryai.app"><strong>support@parryai.app</strong></a>. We read every message and usually reply within 2 business days.
      </p>
      <p>
        To help us sort things out faster, include your device model, your iOS version, and your parry version (find it in Settings, About).
      </p>

      <h2>Common questions</h2>
      <p>
        Answers to the most common questions about parry, pricing, tones, and privacy live in the <a href="/#faq">FAQ</a> on our home page.
      </p>

      <h2>Subscriptions and refunds</h2>
      {/* TODO(android): the billing copy here is iOS-only (Apple Account >
          Subscriptions; refunds via reportaproblem.apple.com). When parry
          ships on Google Play, add the Android equivalent (manage/cancel and
          refunds via Google Play). The data-deletion section below carries
          the same iOS-only cancellation note. */}
      <p>
        Manage or cancel a parry Pro subscription in iOS Settings: tap your name, then Subscriptions. Refunds are handled by Apple, not by parry. Request one at <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Restoring a Pro purchase</h2>
      <p>
        Reinstalled parry, or switched to a new phone? Your Pro subscription is tied to your Apple Account's purchase receipt, not an account, so there is nothing to sign back into. Open the upgrade screen in parry and tap <strong>Restore Purchases</strong>. Your Pro status, your custom tones, and the day's usage count come right back.
      </p>

      <h2>Data deletion</h2>
      <p>
        You can delete your parry data from inside the app. There is no separate website step.
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>Open parry and go to Settings.</li>
        <li>Scroll to the bottom.</li>
        <li>Tap the red <strong>Delete data</strong> link.</li>
        <li>Confirm when the app asks. parry confirms with you before anything is removed.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        This permanently removes your custom tones and your usage history (the metadata we log for each suggestion, such as the tone and timestamp). It cannot be undone. One thing it does not reset: your daily usage count, which is kept as an anonymous tally so that limits can't be refreshed by deleting and reinstalling.
      </p>
      <p>
        Deleting your data does not cancel a paid subscription, since Apple manages billing. Cancel that separately in iOS Settings: tap your name, then Subscriptions.
      </p>
      <p>
        Stuck, or can't reach Settings? Email <a href="mailto:support@parryai.app">support@parryai.app</a> and we'll help you get your data deleted.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy and policies</h2>
      <p>
        Read our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>, <a href="/terms">terms of service</a>, and <a href="/usage">usage policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
